.claude/skills/skillforge-hot/

# Project-scoped knowledge store. Skills are approved per-machine against a
# content hash in trust.json, which is not committed -- so a skill arriving
# through git would land unapproved on every teammate's checkout and sit in
# quarantine anyway. Sharing project skills is a real feature; it needs a
# deliberate export/approve path, not an accident of `git add`.
.claude/skillforge/
# Worktrees created by EnterWorktree; local scratch, never part of a commit.
.claude/worktrees/
